{% comment %}
  Shared step header: back button + facility badge (mobile) / progress
  dots (desktop) + close button, plus the mobile-only step progress bar
  underneath ("STEP X OF 5 / Next: ..." + a fill line). Concern Select
  and Doctor Select both use this exact composition per their Figma specs
  (nodes 544:3648 and 544:3781) — extracted here instead of duplicating
  the markup per step, so every step that reuses this header shares one
  definition (see kal-booking-flow.css's .kal-step-header__* /
  .kal-step-progress-bar__* rules, themselves generalized from what was
  originally Concern Select-only CSS).

  Accepts:
  - back_target: {String} data-kal-back value, e.g. "entry"
  - step_number: {Number} 1-5, which step this is
  - step_total: {Number} total steps, e.g. 5
  - next_label: {String} e.g. "Mode & Doctor", "Date & Time" — ignored on
    the last step (step_number == step_total), which shows a plain
    "Final step" instead of "Next : ..." per the Confirmation step's own
    Figma spec (node 438:7468)
  - location_text: {String} facility name shown in the badge — defaults to
    "Indiranagar" (dummy value, same placeholder used everywhere else in
    this flow until it's wired to a real facility)

  Usage:
  {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-header', back_target: 'entry', step_number: 1, step_total: 5, next_label: 'Mode & Doctor' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign location_text = location_text | default: 'Indiranagar'
  assign step_percent = step_number | times: 100.0 | divided_by: step_total
-%}

<div class="kal-step-doctor-select__header kal-step-shell__header">
  <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back" data-kal-back="{{ back_target }}" aria-label="Back">
    {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-left' -%}
  </button>

  <div class="kal-step-header__location-slot">
    {%- comment -%}
      Mobile: static facility badge. The down chevron is purely visual —
      no data-kal-facility hook, no click handler. Explicit instruction:
      "dont need this dropdown [behavior] just the selected facility
      should be shown" — the chevron stays for visual match, the dropdown
      it implies doesn't actually open anything yet.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-step-header__location-badge">
      <span class="kal-step-header__location-badge-left">
        <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
          {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'location-pin' -%}
        </span>
        <span class="kal-step-header__location-text">{{ location_text }}</span>
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-header__location-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-down' -%}
      </span>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Desktop: unchanged progress dots, hidden below 750px, see CSS {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress">
      {%- for i in (1..step_total) -%}
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot{% if i == step_number %} kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot--active{% endif %}"></span>
      {%- endfor -%}
      <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-text">{{ step_number }}/{{ step_total }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} Own close button — a real flex sibling of back/badge in this row, not the separate, absolutely-positioned .kal-booking-flow__close {%- endcomment -%}
  <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back" data-kal-close aria-label="Close">
    {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'close' -%}
  </button>
</div>

{%- comment -%} Mobile-only step progress bar, replaces the header's progress dots visually at this width — see CSS {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="kal-step-progress-bar">
  <div class="kal-step-progress-bar__labels">
    <span class="kal-step-progress-bar__step">Step {{ step_number }} of {{ step_total }}</span>
    <span class="kal-step-progress-bar__next">
      {%- if step_number == step_total -%}
        Final step
      {%- else -%}
        Next : {{ next_label }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="kal-step-progress-bar__track">
    <div class="kal-step-progress-bar__fill" style="--kal-step-progress: {{ step_percent }}%;"></div>
  </div>
</div>
